Get the highest score per student per year. (Deloitte USI)
Use ROW_NUMBER() partitioned by both student name and year, ordered by score descending. Filter for rn
= 1 to get the top-scoring row per student per year. This covers partition on multiple columns — a common
interview pattern.

WITH RankedScores AS (
SELECT name, year, scores,
ROW_NUMBER() OVER
(PARTITION BY name, year ORDER BY scores DESC) AS rn
FROM scores_table
)
SELECT name, year, scores FROM RankedScores WHERE rn = 1;
